 an ongoing  restriction  or restricting of the base for free  reporting in hong kong each of these  incidents is different in its own way  but together  they paint a pretty clear picture that  you know independent reporting is under  some threat in hong kong this is the  first time a journalist has been put on  trial  for coverage of the anti-government  protests  bow choi has pleaded not guilty but her  supporters fear  her arrest may not be the last sarah  clark  al-jazeera hong kong
 

